KG42.register("rules-53e57165842d2370f985a5dc",{"id":"42-data_center_space_time_flexibility::v141-c-R009","paper":"42-data_center_space_time_flexibility","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R009","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M02","name":"Market payment","process_stage":"settlement","market_meaning":"The flexible consumer is charged using each offered node's price and the corresponding component of its disaggregated load, rather than a single-node price. Scope: Load-disaggregation market with a flexible consumer served across its offered nodes. The nodal-balance expression establishes revenue adequacy of market payments. Scope: Payment accounting for the load-disaggregation clearing formulation (2.16). Condition: For solutions satisfying nodal balance constraints (2.16b) and (2.16c).","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function settlement.payment under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["settlement.payment"],"E":[],"omega":{"market_type":"DEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"settlement","context_text":"Load-disaggregation market with a flexible consumer served across its offered nodes. | Payment accounting for the load-disaggregation clearing formulation (2.16).","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e010","v141-b-g02-e015","v141-b-g02-e016"]},"x":[{"variable_id":"v141-c-R009-X001","symbol":"d_n","meaning":"Disaggregated load delivered to the flexible consumer at offered node n; component of the flexible consumer's cleared load.","kind":"operational","domain":"\\mathbb{R}_+ (source also imposes \\sum_{n\\in N_d} d_n \\le \\bar d)","unit":null,"indices":["n"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e010","v141-b-g02-e015","v141-b-g01-e038"]},{"variable_id":"v141-c-R009-X002","symbol":"p_i","meaning":"Cleared power injection of supplier i appearing in the nodal-balance revenue-adequacy expression.","kind":"operational","domain":"p\\in C_p (source M02 (2.16g); explicit numeric domain not restated in M02)","unit":null,"indices":["i"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e016","v141-b-g01-e039"]},{"variable_id":"v141-c-R009-X003","symbol":"f_k","meaning":"Cleared flow on directed edge k appearing in the nodal-balance revenue-adequacy expression.","kind":"operational","domain":"Directed-edge flow satisfying f_{l^+}-f_{l^-}=B_l(\\theta_{snd(l)}-\\theta_{rec(l)}), l\\in L (M02 (2.16f)); nonnegativity is not restated in M02","unit":null,"indices":["k"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e016","v141-b-g01-e039"]}],"theta":[{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R009-T001","symbol":"\\pi_n","meaning":"Cleared nodal price (LMP) at node n used to charge or remunerate market participants; in this rule it prices the flexible consumer's disaggregated load at each offered node.","value":{"kind":"symbolic","number_value":null,"text_value":"\\pi_n"},"unit":null,"indices":["n"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e010","v141-b-g02-e016"]},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R009-T002","symbol":"\\alpha^d","meaning":"Bid price of the flexible consumer for its requested load; it enters the flexible-consumer profit function as the value of served disaggregated load.","value":{"kind":"symbolic","number_value":null,"text_value":"\\alpha^d"},"unit":null,"indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e010","v141-b-g02-e015","v141-b-g01-e038"]}],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R009-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The flexible consumer is charged using each offered node's price and the corresponding component of its disaggregated load, rather than a single-node price. Scope: Load-disaggregation market with a flexible consumer served across its offered nodes.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["settlement.payment"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e010","v141-b-g02-e015"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R009-C002","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The nodal-balance expression establishes revenue adequacy of market payments. Scope: Payment accounting for the load-disaggregation clearing formulation (2.16). Condition: For solutions satisfying nodal balance constraints (2.16b) and (2.16c).","expression":"0 = \\sum_{n\\in N} \\pi_n \\left( \\sum_{k\\in K^{rec}_n} f_k + \\sum_{i\\in S_n} p_i - \\sum_{k\\in K^{snd}_n} f_k - d_n \\right),\\quad d_n=0\\ \\forall n\\in N\\setminus N_d","formalization_origin":"equivalent_translation","template_id":null,"members":["settlement.payment"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R009-X001","v141-c-R009-X002","v141-c-R009-X003"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R009-T001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e016"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R009-C003","kind":"mathematical","role":"supporting","statement":"The flexible consumer's profit is the bid value of its disaggregated load minus the nodal-price charge at each offered node.","expression":"\\phi^d(\\pi,d) := \\sum_{n\\in N_d} (\\alpha^d - \\pi_n) d_n","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["settlement.payment"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R009-X001"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R009-T001","v141-c-R009-T002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e010","v141-b-g02-e015"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e010","location":{"location_id":"src-1c03246cb9-p06-c1r1__v141-a-M02-pricing","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"2.3 Basic formulation with flexible consumers","anchor_text":"W. Zhang and V.M. Zavala consumer (𝑑) can receive load, while those not offered (⧵𝑑) cannot. The ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"The profit function for the flexible consumer is defined as \\phi^d(\\pi,d):=\\sum_{n\\in N_d}(\\alpha^d-\\pi_n)d_n. This indicates that the consumer is charged for power based on the prices of all the nodes offered. This remuneration mechanism is fundamentally different from that of an inflexible consumer (which is charged based on the price at a single node)."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e015","location":{"location_id":"src-1c03246cb9-p06-c1r4__v141-a-M02-pricing","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"2.3 Basic formulation with flexible consumers","anchor_text":"m s.t. 0 ≤𝑝𝑖≤̄ 𝑝 (2.20b) 𝑑,𝑝 s. ∑ max (𝜋rec(𝑘) −𝜋snd(𝑘) −𝛼𝑓𝑘)𝑓𝑘 (2.21a) 𝑓,𝜃∈𝜃 𝑘∈ s.t. 𝑓𝑙+ −𝑓𝑙−= 𝐵𝑙","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"It is straightforward to show that the profit maximization problems for suppliers (2.20) and transmission providers (2.21) are the same as those of the base formulation with inflexible consumers (under DC constraints). The main difference that arises here lies in the profit maximization problem for the consumer (2.19); the structure of this problem confirms that the flexible consumer should be charged based on the nodal prices and the corresponding components of the disaggregated load; moreover, the total load served should not exceed the requested capacity."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e016","location":{"location_id":"src-1c03246cb9-p06-c2r1__v141-a-M02-settlement","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"2.3 Basic formulation with flexible consumers","anchor_text":"Applied Energy 326 (2022) 119930 𝑑) Market clearance is guaranteed by satisfaction of the power bala","equation_id":"2.22","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Market clearance is guaranteed by satisfaction of the power balance constraints (2.16b), (2.16c). Furthermore, (2.19)-(2.21) show that the formulation (2.16) delivers an optimal price and allocation that maximize profit for the flexible consumer, each of the suppliers, and the transmission network. From the balance constraints (2.16b), (2.16c) we have: 0=\\sum_{n\\in N}\\pi_n\\left(\\sum_{k\\in K^{rec}_n}f_k+\\sum_{i\\in S_n}p_i-\\sum_{k\\in K^{snd}_n}f_k-\\sum_{j\\in D_n}d_j\\right) (2.22). Basic manipulations reveal that this expression implies revenue adequacy."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e038","location":{"location_id":"src-1c03246cb9-p05-c2r3__v141-a-M02-bidding","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"2.3 Basic formulation with flexible consumers","anchor_text":"2) Understanding the effect of transmission capacity on prices will become relevant for the formulat","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"We now expand the previous clearing formulation by incorporating flexible consumers; specifically, we consider flexible consumers that offer load-shifting flexibility by exploiting the availability of multiple DaCes placed at different nodes. For simplicity in the presentation, we consider a single flexible consumer. Suppose that this consumer submits a bid for requested load \\bar{d} with bid price \\alpha^{d}; the requested load can be served/delivered at a set of nodes \\mathcal{N}_{d}\\subseteq\\mathcal{N}. Each node n\\in\\mathcal{N}_{d} receives a partial load d_{n}\\ge 0; the total load served to the consumer is \\sum_{n\\in\\mathcal{N}_{d}}d_{n} and satisfies \\sum_{n\\in\\mathcal{N}_{d}}d_{n}\\le\\bar{d} (total load served cannot exceed the requested load)."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e039","location":{"location_id":"src-1c03246cb9-p05-c2r3__v141-a-M02-clearing","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"2.3 Basic formulation with flexible consumers","anchor_text":"2) Understanding the effect of transmission capacity on prices will become relevant for the formulat","equation_id":"2.16","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"The clearing problem is: \\min_{d,p,f,\\theta} \\sum_{i\\in\\mathcal{S}}\\alpha^{p}_{i}p_{i}+\\sum_{k\\in\\mathcal{K}}\\alpha^{f}_{k}f_{k}-\\alpha^{d}\\sum_{n\\in\\mathcal{N}_{d}}d_{n} \\quad (2.16a) s.t. \\sum_{k\\in\\mathcal{K}^{rec}_{n}}f_{k}+\\sum_{i\\in\\mathcal{S}_{n}}p_{i}=\\sum_{k\\in\\mathcal{K}^{snd}_{n}}f_{k}+d_{n},\\quad (\\pi_n),\\ n\\in\\mathcal{N}_{d} \\quad (2.16b) \\sum_{k\\in\\mathcal{K}^{rec}_{n}}f_{k}+\\sum_{i\\in\\mathcal{S}_{n}}p_{i}=\\sum_{k\\in\\mathcal{K}^{snd}_{n}}f_{k},\\quad (\\pi_n),\\ n\\in\\mathcal{N}\\setminus\\mathcal{N}_{d} \\quad (2.16c) 0\\le\\sum_{n\\in\\mathcal{N}_{d}}d_{n}\\le\\bar{d} \\quad (2.16d) d_{n}\\ge 0,\\quad n\\in\\mathcal{N}_{d} \\quad (2.16e) f_{l^{+}}-f_{l^{-}}=B_{l}(\\theta_{snd(l)}-\\theta_{rec(l)}),\\quad l\\in\\mathcal{L} \\quad (2.16f) p\\in C_{p},\\ \\theta\\in C_{\\theta} \\quad (2.16g)."}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":"C explicitly supplied only source-backed unary facts for this function; other graph gaps remain reviewable.","empty_x_reason":null,"empty_theta_reason":null},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M02-pricing","v141-a-M02-settlement"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"settlement.payment","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e010","quote":"This indicates that the consumer is charged for power based on the prices of all the nodes offered. This remuneration mechanism is fundamentally different from that of an inflexible consumer (which is charged based on the price at a single node)."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e015","quote":"the structure of this problem confirms that the flexible consumer should be charged based on the nodal prices and the corresponding components of the disaggregated load"}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e016","quote":"Market clearance is guaranteed by satisfaction of the power balance constraints (2.16b), (2.16c)."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e016","quote":"Basic manipulations reveal that this expression implies revenue adequacy."}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"29c607642a504004c073263335850b140ae857e47191cc4ad18043e3d63bc67d","applicability":"formalized","reason":"The source provides an explicit flexible-consumer profit function, phi^d(pi,d)=sum_{n in N_d}(alpha^d-pi_n)d_n, which directly supports the nodal-price charge exposure. It also provides the nodal-balance identity (2.22) used to establish revenue adequacy. C001 remains a procedural narrative because the source does not define a separate charge variable; C002 is formalized as the M02 nodal-balance form of (2.22), and C003 transcribes the profit/payment expression. B evidence remains unreviewed, and the notation in (2.22) is handled as an explicit M02 translation.","bindings":[{"object_id":"v141-c-R009-X001","node_ids":["settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"d_n is the disaggregated load component multiplied by each offered node's price in the flexible-consumer payment/profit expression (source e010 and e015)."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R009-X002","node_ids":["settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"p_i appears in the nodal-balance identity (2.22) used to establish revenue adequacy of settlement.payment."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R009-X003","node_ids":["settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"f_k appears in the nodal-balance identity (2.22) used to establish revenue adequacy of settlement.payment."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R009-T001","node_ids":["settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"pi_n is the nodal price used in the flexible-consumer profit/payment expression and in the revenue-adequacy nodal-balance identity."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R009-T002","node_ids":["settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"alpha^d is the flexible consumer's bid price in the profit expression, where it sets the value against which nodal-price charges are netted in settlement.payment."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R009-C002","node_ids":["settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"Source e016 uses the nodal-balance expression (2.22) to establish revenue adequacy for the load-disaggregation formulation. Source (2.22) quotes the aggregate load as \\sum_{j\\in D_n} d_j; in M02 the single flexible consumer's balances (2.16b)-(2.16c) carry d_n at n in N_d and no d_n elsewhere, so C002 uses the equivalent M02 notation with d_n and d_n=0 outside N_d."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R009-C003","node_ids":["settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"Exact source profit function phi^d(pi,d)=sum_{n in N_d}(alpha^d-pi_n)d_n decomposes into bid value minus nodal-price charge and characterizes the charge/remuneration relation of settlement.payment."}],"revision_requests":["Confirm the intended notation in B evidence v141-b-g02-e016: the quoted (2.22) uses \\sum_{j\\in D_n} d_j while M02 balance constraints (2.16b)-(2.16c) use d_n. C002 uses the M02 nodal-balance form with d_n=0 outside N_d.","If C001 is to be formalized directly as a charge rather than via the profit function, provide a source-defined charge symbol; the present source defines phi^d, not a separate charge variable."]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
